      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "68. He is a son who pleases his father with good actions;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "that is a wife who desires the good alone of her husband;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "that is a friend who acts the same way in adversity as in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "happy times. The meritorious ( alone ) secure these three",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "things in this world.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "69. Rising by bending low ( i. e. by their humility ), evi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "dencing their own merits by extolling those of others,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "gaining their ends by projecting extensive schemes for ( the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "good of ) others, and censuring calumniators, whose tongues",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "( lit. mouths ) are noisy with harsh syllables of accusation,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with their patience alone—virtuous men of such extraor-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "dinary behaviour and highly esteemed in the world—who",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "will not adore them ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "70. Trees become bent ( i. e. humble ) with the harvest",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of fruits; with newly-formed waters the clouds hang very",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "low; good men with ( the acquisition of ) wealth become",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "meek; this is the nature of benevolent persons.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "71. The ear is graced by Vedic knowledge alone, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "not by an ear-ring; the hand by charity, not by a bracelet;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the body of beneficent people by kindness towards others,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and not by sandal-paint.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "72. Wise people thus describe the characteristics of a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "true friend;—he ( i. e. a good friend ) dissuades (you) from",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "sin, urges (you) to good action, keeps (your) secrets, publi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "shes (your) merits, does not forsake you (when you are) in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "distress, and helps ( you, lit. gives you ) in time of need.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "73. The sun causes the group of son-lotuses to expand",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "without a solicitation; the moon, though unasked, causes the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "moon-lotuses to bloom; and the cloud yields water without",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "being solicited; good people direct their efforts towards the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "good of others of their owd accord.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
